# {{ plugin_name }}

A stereo gain effect with click-free smoothing, bypass and sample-accurate
parameter events. Start here for a small audio effect.

An independent RVST {{ kind }} plugin by {{ vendor }}. You own the processor,
shared editor, native wrappers and build tools in this repository.

## First run

Run commands from this repository's root. The included `rust-toolchain.toml`
selects Rust 1.98.0, rustfmt and Clippy. Native builds also need your platform's
compiler and audio/window libraries; see the
[native setup guide](https://github.com/S33G/rvst/blob/main/docs/getting-started.md).
{% if sdk_source == "registry" %}
This project's registry SDK must be published before these commands can build;
see [SDK and plugin identity](#sdk-and-plugin-identity) for the source alternative.
{% endif %}
```sh
cargo run -p plugin-standalone --locked --features devtools -- --tone 220
```

Start at low volume. The runner feeds a 220 Hz test tone into the effect;
move Gain, Smoothing and Bypass to hear the changes. For a WAV input instead,
replace `--tone 220` with `--file /path/to/input.wav`.

The standalone uses your default audio output. It does not open a microphone
or physical MIDI devices. Close its window to stop it.

