## Build, bundle and install

| Command | Result |
| --- | --- |
| `cargo build --locked` | Compiles the workspace; no plugin installation |
| `cargo xtask bundle --release` | Builds VST3 and CLAP bundles under Cargo's `target/bundled/` |
| `cargo xtask install` | Builds development bundles and copies them to your user plugin folders |
| `cargo xtask install --release` | Builds and installs release bundles |

Use `bundle vst3` or `bundle clap` to select one format. Bundle/install also
accept `--target`, `--profile` or `--features`; use either `--release` or
`--profile`. The command prints the resulting paths. After installing, rescan
plugins in your DAW. Validate the bundles and test real DAW sessions before
shipping; compilation and unit tests do not establish host compatibility.

Regular development uses Cargo:

```sh
cargo test --workspace --locked
cargo fmt --all --check
cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings
```

## Preview the editor in a browser

Install the WASM target and the CLI version matching this project's lockfile:

```sh
rustup target add wasm32-unknown-unknown
cargo install wasm-bindgen-cli --version 0.2.130 --locked
cargo xtask web --serve --open
```

This runs the same Rust editor against a simulated host. It previews controls,
themes and parameter state; it does not process browser audio. Stop the server
with Ctrl+C. If the `wasm-bindgen` dependency changes, match its CLI version too.

## Inspect native logs and reproduce processing

With the first-run command still running, follow the native inspector link in
the editor or open the URL printed in the terminal. It shows native logs,
parameters and callback metrics. With the optional `cargo-rvst` tool installed,
you can also discover running instances from another terminal:

```sh
cargo rvst inspect --open
```

Choose **Echo new logs to DevTools** in the inspector to view new native events
in Chrome's Console. For native source breakpoints, use the supplied
[CodeLLDB launch/attach configurations](.vscode/launch.json).

To record and replay a deterministic **offline test fixture**:

```sh
cargo xtask record capture.json --blocks 64
cargo xtask replay capture.json --step
```

Use a new output filename for each recording. This fixture exercises processing
and block boundaries; it is not a recording of the running DAW or standalone app.

## Change the sound and appearance

Edit [plugin-core](crates/plugin-core/src/lib.rs) for processor behavior. Keep
allocations, blocking calls and I/O off the audio callback.

The [shared editor](crates/plugin-ui/src/lib.rs) currently calls
`rvst_ui::default_editor`. Try the bundled Dark, Light and Studio skins in the
editor, then replace that call with your own Rust layout. The
{% if sdk_source == "vendor/rvst" %}[theme guide](vendor/rvst/docs/themes.md){% else %}[theme guide](https://github.com/S33G/rvst/blob/main/docs/themes.md){% endif %} explains token manifests, fonts and SVG artwork.
Keep platform services outside this shared editor so it can run in every host.

## SDK and plugin identity

SDK source: `{{ sdk_source }}`.

{% if sdk_source == "vendor/rvst" %}The SDK snapshot lives in [vendor/rvst](vendor/rvst). Commit it with this
repository: a clone builds without the original RVST checkout or a global
`cargo-rvst` installation. Rust and the other Cargo dependencies are still
required; the SDK snapshot does not vendor crates.io dependencies.
{% elsif sdk_source == "registry" %}This project uses registry dependencies. It needs a published, compatible RVST
release; RVST 0.1.0 is currently unpublished. Until publication, generate a new
project with `--sdk-path /path/to/rvst --vendor-sdk` for a portable SDK snapshot.
{% else %}This project uses absolute development paths to an RVST checkout. A clone still
needs that checkout at the recorded path, or updated dependency paths. To make
a portable project at generation time, use `--sdk-path /path/to/rvst --vendor-sdk`.
{% endif %}

Keep [rvst-project.json](rvst-project.json) for generation provenance. The
[workspace manifest](Cargo.toml) records the bundle name and plugin ID;
[plugin-core](crates/plugin-core/src/lib.rs) contains the descriptor and VST3
class ID. After release, preserve the plugin ID, VST3 class ID and parameter IDs,
even if you rename the display name. Hosts use these identities to restore
existing sessions and automation.
